# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local runtime memory — never committed (this repository has a public remote)
#
# `data/` holds who he is and what he has done: conversation transcripts, the
# per-month episode log, the learned-memory store, the day log, and the 48-slot
# calendar. The files ARE the memory, and they live on this machine only.
#
# These rules matter across BOTH eras: the working tree is shared, so switching
# branches leaves this directory on disk. A few names below belong to the
# `pi-native` branch's file format — they are listed here so that checking out
# that branch can never leave private memory one `git add -A` from the remote.
#
# Deliberately still tracked: `data/past_linkedin_posts/*.txt` (the voice
# corpus) and `data/telegram_offset.json` (a chat cursor). Tracked files are
# unaffected by ignore rules, so nothing below untracks them.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
data/conversations/
data/episodes/
data/schedule/
data/memories.jsonl
data/daylog.jsonl
data/requests.jsonl
data/attention.jsonl
data/.curator_cursor.json
data/README.md
